  "package_content_hash": "9b238fcd88e9a10769a82dc6f8b013825f75d857e2053ac978c93daa443ce728",
  "package_id": "continuity_initiative",
  "scene": "3B",
  "transcript_lines": [
    "Kristin traces the forced entry, overturned chair, missing tablet and work bag, and Michelle\u2019s undamaged phone to a removal too deliberate to be looting.",
    "A memory card is taped beneath the KMS drawer. Michelle left it there.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands. A federal emergency patrol pulls up outside Michelle's house. Two officers get out. One walks to the front door. The other looks over the street.",
    "The card holds Michelle's saved files and a damaged recording. The recording warns, \"Do not trust the emergency broadcasts.\" The files name the Continuity Initiative and point to a dead drop at a bench in the park. The front door opens. An officer walks in and heads straight for Michelle's workstation.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands. The patrol pulls away from the curb.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands. The patrol is coming back to the house. Kristin starts the truck and heads for the park, avoiding checkpoints and emergency patrols. The park was quieter than the streets around it. The clues led Kristin to an ordinary bench near the service path. She crossed the damaged grounds, kept clear of the checkpoints, and knelt beside the bench.",
    "Kristin reaches beneath the park bench. She retrieves a transit token, a handwritten number sequence and Michelle's photograph. She keeps all three with her.",
    "The man says his name is Brandon Corfman. He says the missing people are being moved alive. A tactical team is closing across the park. Brandon says he can open the secured service gate beside the storm drain. He tells Kristin to follow him.",
    "As patrols close in, Brandon opens a secured service gate. He leads Kristin through it.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands. The park pursuit was behind them. Kristin and Brandon headed for the freight terminal along the transport route. Michelle's lead brought Kristin and Brandon to the freight terminal. It was supposed to be abandoned. Fresh tire tracks crossed the loading docks. The air vents hummed. Brandon said, \"Check the loading docks for signs of activity. The observation shaft gives us a view below. Let's find out what is happening before we try to get inside.\"",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "Kristin finds electrical load, fresh air from the vents, and signs of recent work. The freight terminal is still running. Brandon says, \"Study the people through the observation shaft. We need to know what is happening on the processing line.\"",
    "Kristin studies the sedated prisoners through the observation shaft. They are alive. Brandon says, \"Copy the prisoner numbers if you want stronger proof. Or ask me about the transfer route. I can help with the service entrance. That will cost us the chance to copy the full set of numbers. There is time for one choice before the transfer leaves.\"",
    "Kristin copies the visible prisoner numbers and matches them to missing-person records. Brandon says, \"That gives us stronger proof. We still need a way inside.\" Kristin and Brandon withdraw from the terminal to prepare a way inside. One night in Brandon's hideout had turned years of leaked Continuity Initiative documents into two inspector badges and a work order for a cooling-water fault. Now the badges had to work. Kristin and Brandon stood at the facility gate while a shift supervisor walked out to meet them, reading the work order with a frown. \"Nobody scheduled you,\" he said.\n\nKristin still has the copied prisoner numbers. The codes on the supervisor's work orders look like the same system.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "Kristin proves that the genuine cooling-water pressure fault is real. She finds a ventilation fault. The shift supervisor grants access to the restricted infrastructure corridors. The limited console can report faults and cycle noncritical systems. It cannot open detention cells or change the main flood controls. The supervisor left them at the inspection console in the infrastructure corridors. Behind it, the cooling-service panel led into the records archive. Kristin and Brandon came through the cooling-service panel into the records archive just as the lights came up at the far end. An audit sweep had started. Voices and footsteps were working their way down the aisles toward them. They had a few minutes among the archive terminals.\n\nThe supervisor had logged them at the gate, and the audit sweep had started early because of it. The voices were already close, working down the nearest aisle. Kristin and Brandon had barely a minute among the archive terminals.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "Kristin pulls her own file first. It says she was retained to lead investigators to Corfman. Kristin was bait. The file names the system JANUS. The build record names Brandon Corfman as an author. Brandon admits that he helped write JANUS. He says he tried to stop it after he learned its purpose. Kristin keeps his name in the record. The JANUS files are copied. Kristin carries the copied files.",
    "Kristin types one reply to the maintenance line. Michelle answers once. She is alive. She is working inside the facility. She will send a route. Kristin and Brandon slipped out of the archive with the copied files. In the command corridor beyond, doors were already closing at both ends. Guards closed the command corridor at both ends. Then a woman in an executive's suit walked between them, unhurried, a tablet under her arm. She looked at Brandon first. \"I wondered when you'd come back,\" said Rebecca Jenkins. Kristin still carried the copied JANUS files.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "Rebecca offers a way to remove Charles. She promises Michelle's release. The purge order starts a clock. Kristin heads to the uplink and starts sending the copied files. The detention sectors seal. Michelle's route leads to Rebecca's secured office. The office can broadcast the evidence and open the detention cells. The purge clock was running. Michelle's route led down into the detention levels, and the plan was now one combined mission: broadcast the truth and free the captives. A partly unsecured detention sector opened onto rows of captives. Coded announcements crackled through stolen radios, and the prisoners moved with a discipline no captor had taught them - someone inside had been organizing this long before rescue arrived.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "Kristin finds Michelle alive. Michelle is directing the prisoners through stolen radios and coded announcements. Michelle points toward the medical level, where the experiment records wait.",
    "Michelle shows Kristin the medical level. The prisoners were subjected to memory, compliance, and resistance experiments. The senior official waits among the government prisoners.",
    "The senior official Charles framed gives Kristin one-use authority for the emergency surface gates. It expires when Charles activates his new authority. Michelle turns toward the prisoners at the checkpoints.",
    "Michelle triggers the coordinated uprising. The prisoners seize checkpoints and open a fighting route toward the command and broadcast levels.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands. Michelle's uprising disabled cameras and seized checkpoints, while Charles sealed the primary exits and sent armed teams downward. Kristin, Michelle, and Brandon fought upward through the security corridors. Alarms layered over alarms as the facility fought to predict its attackers. Water-pressure warnings flashed on the inspection console while doors opened and closed in empty service corridors that JANUS watched move by move.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "A concrete authored consequence lands.",
    "Kristin feeds JANUS false alarms. Human operators take control. Rebecca's executive office waits beyond the security corridors.",
